{
 "title": "Why tilt beats distance",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Zoom in on July",
   "say": "Yes, in July Earth is farthest from the Sun, but the North Pole tilts right toward it.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_left",
     "x": 190,
     "y": 480,
     "w": 180,
     "h": 220,
     "color": "blue",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_far",
     "x": 200,
     "y": 710,
     "text": "July (aphelion):\nFarthest from Sun,\nNorth tilts IN",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Angle of sunlight",
